<title>UK: Imperial Tobacco sees no job losses at Rizla.</title>
<headline>Imperial Tobacco sees no job losses at Rizla.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Tobacco Group Plc said on Tuesday that it did not expect any job losses to result from its 168 million stg acquisition of Rizla International BV.</p>
<p>In a telephone interview with Reuters, Imperial Tobacco chief executive Gareth Davis said he will be &quot;looking a the business closely,&quot; but added &quot;we are not foreseeing job losses&quot; among the company's 714 employees.  </p>
<p>&quot;We do see scope for productivity improvements, but the plants are working at capacity,&quot; Davis said.</p>
<p>Rizla, based in the Netherlands, has production facilities in Belgium, Wales and southern France.</p>
<p>--Jonathan Birt London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
